# POST /api/auth/register is AdminOnly: 401 without a session, 403 for a plain mechanic (before the body is validated),
# and the CSRF double-submit applies to an admin session too. No case creates an account.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@TestPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_PASSWORD}}
@AdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@AdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@NonAdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_EMAIL}}
@NonAdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_PASSWORD}}
@RunId = {{$timestamp}}


### [Setup][Auth] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Negative][Register] Unauthenticated registration (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Blocked", "lastName": "Unauth", "email": "blocked.unauth.{{RunId}}@example.test", "password": "{{TestPassword}}", "personType": "Mechanic", "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel", "expertise": ["Engine"] }

?? status == 401

###

### [Setup][Admin Session] Login as admin (200 expected)
# @name Login
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{AdminEmail}}", "password": "{{AdminPassword}}" }

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('__Host-arsm-csrf-token='))?.match(/^__Host-arsm-csrf-token=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Negative][Register] An admin session without X-CSRF-Token is refused before the handler (403 expected, csrf_token_invalid)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Blocked", "lastName": "NoCsrf", "email": "blocked.nonadmin.csrf.{{RunId}}@example.test", "password": "{{TestPassword}}", "personType": "Mechanic", "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel", "expertise": ["Engine"] }

?? status == 403
?? js response.parsedBody.code == csrf_token_invalid

###

### [Setup][Admin Session] Logout admin before the non-admin check (204 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204

###

### [Setup][Non-Admin Session] Login as the plain mechanic (200 expected, isAdmin false)
# @name Login
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{NonAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{NonAdminPassword}}" }

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('__Host-arsm-csrf-token='))?.match(/^__Host-arsm-csrf-token=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.isAdmin == false

###

# The CSRF token is sent on purpose: without it the 403 below would come from CsrfDoubleSubmitMiddleware, not AdminOnly.

### [Negative][Register] A plain mechanic cannot register mechanics (403 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Blocked", "lastName": "NonAdmin", "email": "blocked.nonadmin.{{RunId}}@example.test", "password": "{{TestPassword}}", "personType": "Mechanic", "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel", "expertise": ["Engine"] }

?? status == 403

###

### [Negative][Register] Authorization precedes validation: an invalid body is still 403 for a plain mechanic (403 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "", "lastName": "", "email": "", "password": "", "personType": "Customer" }

?? status == 403

###

### [Setup][Non-Admin Session] Logout the plain mechanic (204 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204
